12047 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The liquidate\137loan\050\051 function allows a loan that was previously redeemed to be liquidated if its LTV is greater than liquidation\137ltv \050the liquidation threshold\051\056\nHowever\054 the LTV calculation still uses loan\056collateral\137amount as the current collateral and loan\056amount \053 current\137interest as the current debt\054 even though these values are not updated after redemption\056 After redemption\054 a portion of the collateral is converted into payment tokens at a previous rate\054 which may differ from the current rate\056\nAs a result\054 a loan that should be healthy after redemption could still be liquidated because the calculation relies on the original collateral and debt amounts\056 Even if the redemption payment tokens are sufficient to fully cover the debt\054 the loan could still be liquidated\054 causing a loss to the borrower\056)
     /K [ 23 ]
     /P 12048 0 R
     /Pg 9282 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

